message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Quiltwright: Holographic Output for Looking Glass Displays"
abstract: >
  Quiltwright renders multi-view quilts for Looking Glass light-field
  displays. Every view uses an off-axis (asymmetric-frustum) projection
  rather than a toe-in rotation, which is the geometric requirement for the
  display's lenticular optics to fuse the views into stable depth. Scenes
  can come from PyVista/VTK or from the POV-Ray ray-tracer, and the library
  provides tools for managing the holographic depth budget — adjacent-view
  disparity and focal-plane placement — plus a client for Looking Glass
  Bridge and encoders for quilt video and Hololuminescent Display masters.
